	<Desc>8sed math to scale the 8-gon
Side lengths. A regular 16-gon has side 2·sin(11.25°) ≈ 0.390181. A regular octagon has side 2·sin(22.5°) ≈ 0.765367.
Scale factor. To make the octagon's side equal the 16-gon's side, multiply the octagon by sin(11.25°)/sin(22.5°) = 1/(2·cos(11.25°)) ≈ 0.509796.
Final product. 0.509796 × 5.95 ≈ 3.03328.
If the circle were instead inscribed in the polygons (radius 1 as the apothem), the sides would be 0.397825 and 0.828427, and the scale factor would be ≈ 0.480217.</Desc>
